{"author":{"id":"08468221db090fa9af39e58d6a9b2c05540151ac002b313cdfc0777721169c7d"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1789641314,"nonce":"mFrflBMLLQDw0FIQizJhGzcocU0=","target":"1963260c88bad7800c0ae112c5a6094f2028e1306fb0a3aef976c631f7408ac5","message":"Get `firmware/rig_firmware` running on the real board and calibrated.\n\n1. Flash with Partition Scheme \"Huge APP\".\n   FQBN: `esp32:esp32:esp32s3:CDCOnBoot=cdc,FlashMode=qio,FlashSize=16M,PSRAM=opi,PartitionScheme=huge_app`\n   arduino-cli: `/Applications/Arduino IDE.app/Contents/Resources/app/lib/backend/resources/arduino-cli`\n2. Configure over the serial console: `ssid=`, `pass=`, `server=ws://\u003claptop-ip\u003e:3000/ws`.\n   The laptop IP drifts (192.168.0.3 at planning time, 192.168.0.8 at the last server run).\n   Check with `ipconfig getifaddr en0` immediately before setting it, and add a DHCP\n   reservation on the router so it stops moving before fair day.\n3. Run the 16-step no-water bench test in `firmware/README.md`. Confirm the safety rules:\n   no relay energised at boot, valve cap 600 s, pump default 20 s / max 300 s per command,\n   pump refuses with all valves closed and stops when the last valve closes,\n   latched leak refuses valve-on until `reset_leak`, `!` / `all_off` work everywhere.\n4. Run `cal` with water flowing and no leak, to set the per-sensor pulse calibration.\n5. Induce a real leak and tune the `LEAK_*` #defines in `firmware/rig_firmware/config.h`\n   until detection is reliable without false positives.\n\nDepends on the diagnostic-log interpretation issue.","files":null}]}